01:55:42,460 --> 01:55:42,640
All right.

383
01:55:42,640 --> 01:55:51,080
So this fiscal markets hypothesis tells

384
01:55:51,080 --> 01:55:52,260
that returns are unpredictable.

385
01:55:52,260 --> 01:55:54,800
So you can't use past returns to forecast future returns.

386
01:55:55,580 --> 01:55:58,560
But there is a literature on mean reversion,

387
01:55:59,000 --> 01:56:00,660
which is essentially the opposite

388
01:56:00,660 --> 01:56:01,840
of what a normal person thinks.

389
01:56:02,580 --> 01:56:04,980
So the normal view is something like good years follow good

390
01:56:04,980 --> 01:56:06,520
years, bad years follow bad years.

391
01:56:07,020 --> 01:56:08,720
Mean reversion actually says the opposite.

392
01:56:09,060 --> 01:56:10,060
Mean reversion says, no, no, no.

393
01:56:10,060 --> 01:56:12,680
If anything, bad years follow good years,

394
01:56:12,680 --> 01:56:14,120
and good years follow bad years.

395
01:56:14,380 --> 01:56:16,180
And you should buy the stuff that's been doing poorly.

396
01:56:16,600 --> 01:56:18,180
So essentially the reverse of my dad's view,

397
01:56:18,180 --> 01:56:19,760
there's like the fundamentally good companies

398
01:56:19,760 --> 01:56:20,840
and the fundamentally should buy those.

399
01:56:20,840 --> 01:56:22,940
No. The fundamentally good companies are the ones to sell.

400
01:56:22,940 --> 01:56:25,920
And the fundamentally bad companies are the ones to buy,

401
01:56:26,620 --> 01:56:28,460
would be a way of saying it.

402
01:56:28,460 --> 01:56:31,420
So essentially it says that if markets have done poorly

403
01:56:31,420 --> 01:56:34,420
for a while, then on average they will actually do better

404
01:56:34,420 --> 01:56:35,740
or at least individual stocks.

405
01:56:36,480 --> 01:56:39,400
So now if you take a look at what had happened

406
01:56:39,400 --> 01:56:43,340
to U.S. stock markets since around 2009, well,

407
01:56:43,340 --> 01:56:45,360
let's see you had an incredible horrible crash,

408
01:56:45,660 --> 01:56:46,940
and then you've got a bunch of good years.

409
01:56:47,700 --> 01:56:49,880
Right? And the mean reversion story is generally something

